verify-claims stamps walk_verdict: "unavailable" on every finding from the
STRUCTURAL propagator. The propagator does it deliberately and its comment says
why: blank would conflate "no walk was possible" with "this record predates the
field". flows_from_payload rebuilt each row from an EXPLICIT key list, and
walk_verdict / walk_blocked_by were not in it.

So every adjudication packet ever built from this collector printed an N-hop
route and silently withheld the statement that no dataflow walk ran and the
route is call-graph reachability rather than a demonstrated value route.
Measurement 0006's own sample/sample-112.json has neither key, so its two
independent 16-agent panels judged 112 situations without it; a later blind
panel spent its whole effort refuting a 16-hop rabbitmq route the tool had
already flagged as unwalked. Their verdicts stand -- the rubric says judge the
SOURCE and treat the route as a hint -- but the effort was wasted and the
share of the population resting on no walk at all was hidden: 72.3%
structural against 1.5% with a confirmed dependence, on the 16-repo cohort.

CARRIED FAITHFULLY, NOT DEFAULTED. A change that stamped every row
"unavailable" would satisfy the obvious test and be worse than the bug: it
would label as unwalked the 1.5% of findings that carry a confirmed
dependence. An absent field stays None, because a map written before the field
existed made no claim about the walk. Four tests including that control, plus
an end-to-end re-collect showing the three values surviving distinctly:
structural -> unavailable, ddg_mixed -> not_attempted, ddg -> confirmed.

THIS RELOCATES THE DEFECT, and the first diagnosis is recorded because it was
wrong. The blind panels objected that a route was fictitious, which read as the
tool asserting a route it had not established. It does not: verify-claims
discloses the basis and taint.py documents `path` as "ONE call-graph route ...
a witness, not 'the path'". The harness lost it.

Three candidate fixes were priced and dropped first:
  - hop-level argument check: NO call-site argument provenance exists. Across
    220 call-edge construction sites every `args` field is decorator parsing.
  - filter on analysis_method: BACKWARDS. structural is 35.4% precise against
    ddg_mixed's 18.8% on the adjudicated survivors -- a third population
    reproducing 0006's "analysis_method REVERSES between populations".
  - full interprocedural dataflow: ADR-0017 section 4, whose refutation payoff
    measurements 0007 and 0008 already put at zero.

Discharges measurement 0006 defect family F, "the measurement's own packet
builder, NOT hypergumbo. Fix before reuse", for the field that mattered most.
The script had no tests at all before this.

